  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-31T10:26:59.104Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hi there, \nI've noticed that VRC doesn't have a way to show how loud your microphone actually is. You have to either trust you've set things correctly or bother a friend with testing it out.. which doesn't always lead to optimal results. \nIf you're like me and have hearing impairments or something else affecting how you speak, it can also be difficult to check the volume of your voice vs microphone level once you think you've adjusted it correctly only to find out you're still very loud. \nI'm tired of people complaining behind my back that I'm too loud or too quiet.. can you please consider implementing this feature? It's such a basic thing to have, pretty much every game has it as well as Discord Skype etc. Why it's not currently available is confusing.",
